From 0113f4a43760c72b332ea24e9c6d1cc94fcbb0b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nickk19 <nikko8204@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:27:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Display13 eDP: keep the firmware-trained panel link
 (-wex-edp-keep)

The donor answers the first mode set of the boot panel with a complete
mode set: disableDisplay stops the link the firmware trained and
LightUpEDP trains it again. On the Lenovo IdeaPad Slim 5 14IAH8
(i5-12450H, 46A3) its Samsung ATNA40CT01 1920x1200 OLED never completes
that training: clock recovery locks, channel equalization fails with
TPS4 and TPS3 in either pattern order ("Phase 2 of link training
failed"), and the panel stays dark.

With -wex-edp-keep, hook hwRegsNeedUpdate (Tahoe TGL framebuffer, entry
address and prologue checked) and answer "no update" when
- the path is the boot path WEX adopted at the firmware handoff, on the
  panel's Combo DDI and pipe A,
- the firmware's eDP SST source still runs (AlderLakeN::dpSource on a
  fresh readout) and TRANSCONF is enabled and active,
- the pipe already has the requested active size and PIPESRC, and the
  requested lane count and depth.
The donor's own same-mode branch then switches only the plane and scaler
to its surface ("Partial modeset by updating plane/scaler"), leaves the
path attached and returns success; the link is never stopped, as with
NootedGreen's firmware-link mode and Linux i915 fastboot. Anything else
keeps the donor's answer. The link rate is not compared: the same-mode
branch does not touch the DPLL, the DDI or the M/N values. The panel's
Combo port can still have the handoff's native mode 0, so the decision
accepts it on display13PanelBootPort's terms.

So that the donor requests the firmware's format, the switch also caps
the panel's receiver caps at HBR in every view getDPCDInfo and the link
setup read (MAX_LINK_RATE, extended caps, SUPPORTED_LINK_RATES and the
LINK_BW_SET read back), which gives a 1920x1200@60 mode the firmware's
two lanes, and reports the panel EDID's depth and the mode set's
maximum as 8 bpc. Nothing is written to the sink.

WEXEDPKeepFirst and WEXEDPKeep record the first and last decisions
(reasons bitmask, live and requested registers, DPCD lane status),
WEXEDPKeepReady the hook. The firmware must leave the panel at its
native timing: OpenCore UEFI > Output > Resolution = Max.

Display sleep, a resolution change or system sleep still make the donor
retrain the link and leave the panel dark; README lists the limitation.

Tested on the IdeaPad Slim 5 14IAH8 with macOS Tahoe 26.7.1: the first
decision keeps the link and the desktop runs with Metal
(AppleIntelTGLGraphicsMTLDriver), 1080p video and the hardware cursor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
